height: inherit; text-decoration: inherit;" class=3D"">FCRA 623 (a)(3)</spa=
n></span><br><br>Closed Accounts - If a furnisher reports information to a =
CRA on a regular basis, the furnisher must notify the CRA that a consumer h=
as voluntarily closed an=0Aaccount the next time they send information that=
 would normally include that account. This is important because some users =
of information may interpret a closed account as an indicator of bad credit=
 unless the furnisher clearly discloses that the consumer, not the creditor=
, closed the account. <span style=3D"color: inherit; font-size: 14px; font-=
weight: bold; line-height: inherit; text-decoration: inherit;" class=3D"">F=
CRA 623(a)(4)</span><br><br>Delinquent Accounts - When a furnisher refers a=
n account for collection and notifies a CRA that they have done so, they al=
so must report the date of delinquency to the CRA within 90 days. The date =
of delinquency is the month and year the consumer's delinquency resulting i=
n the referral began. <br><br></span></div>=0A<br style=3D"font-size: 17px;=
