px; outline: none; padding: 0px; border: none;"><br></blockquote><blockquot=
e style=3D"margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; outline: none; padding: 0px; border: n=
one; font-size: 17px;">Bruce, the two options above help us to understand w=
hy it is critical to request the date of first delinquency in the debt vali=
dation letter to the collection agency. It also helps us to see why re-agin=
g an account is=0Aillegal. Once a collection agency gets an account, either=
 from the original creditor or another collection agency, they sometimes tr=
y to illegally change dates to restart the statute of limitations as well a=
s the reporting period in an attempt to force a consumer to pay the debt or=
 extend the time period for which they can sue. Please note that if the dat=
e of first delinquency is changed by a collection agency or any creditor, t=
his will directly affect the credit score in a negative way because it will=
 appear as if the delinquent or negative account is newer than it actually =
